Further, the guidelines have been reiterated by the Constitution Bench of Hon'ble Supreme Court in a case titled as National Insurance Company vs. Pranay Sethi & Ors.,
decided on _____________________________________________________________ MACP No.928/19;
31.10.2017, laying down the general principles for computation of compensation in death cases.

Basically only three facts need to be established by the claimants for assessing compensation in the case of death:
(a) age of the deceased;
(b) income of the deceased; and (c) the number of dependents.
